    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nThis seems like a relatively niche feature which can mostly be covered by mapping. There are at least two options here:\r\n- `vim.keymap.set('n', 'gco', 'jgcck', { remap = true })` - which is basically saying \"Go down - toggle line comment - go up\". This moves cursor to the first non-blank character, though (which might be acceptable).\r\n- `vim.keymap.set('n', 'gco', \"<Cmd>lua local l = vim.fn.line('.') + 1; MiniComment.toggle_lines(l, l)<CR>\")` - which is basically saying \"Toggle comment on the next line only\".\r\n\r\nBoth of them won't properly work on the last line and won't support dot-repeat, but still are fairly good solutions.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for suggestion!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This seems like a relatively niche feature which can mostly be covered by mapping. There are at least two options here:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">vim.keymap.set('n', 'gco', 'jgcck', { remap = true })</code> - which is basically saying \"Go down - toggle line comment - go up\". This moves cursor to the first non-blank character, though (which might be acceptable).</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">vim.keymap.set('n', 'gco', \"&lt;Cmd&gt;lua local l = vim.fn.line('.') + 1; MiniComment.toggle_lines(l, l)&lt;CR&gt;\")</code> - which is basically saying \"Toggle comment on the next line only\".</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Both of them won't properly work on the last line and won't support dot-repeat, but still are fairly good solutions.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Thanks for suggestion!\nThis seems like a relatively niche feature which can mostly be covered by mapping. There are at least two options here:\n\nvim.keymap.set('n', 'gco', 'jgcck', { remap = true }) - which is basically saying \"Go down - toggle line comment - go up\". This moves cursor to the first non-blank character, though (which might be acceptable).\nvim.keymap.set('n', 'gco', \"<Cmd>lua local l = vim.fn.line('.') + 1; MiniComment.toggle_lines(l, l)<CR>\") - which is basically saying \"Toggle comment on the next line only\".\n\nBoth of them won't properly work on the last line and won't support dot-repeat, but still are fairly good solutions.",
